# Authentication & Authorization

## Stack

- **NextAuth v5** (`next-auth@5.0.0-beta.31`) with JWT strategy, 7-day max age.
- Providers: Google OAuth + Credentials (bcrypt).
- Config in `src/lib/auth.ts` — exports `auth`, `signIn`, `signOut`, `handlers`.

## Roles

Three roles: `buyer` | `producer` | `admin`.

## Auth checks

```typescript
const session = await auth();

// Authentication
if (!session?.user) return Response.json({ error: "Unauthorized" }, { status: 401 });

// Authorization
if (session.user.role !== "admin") throw new ForbiddenError("Admin access required");

// Ownership
if (resource.producerId.toString() !== session.user.id) throw new ForbiddenError();
```

## Review checklist

- [ ] Every protected endpoint checks `auth()`.
- [ ] Role-based access enforced at service layer, not just UI.
- [ ] Token expiry and refresh handled.
- [ ] CSRF protection on state-changing operations.
- [ ] Session data doesn't leak sensitive fields.
- [ ] Failed auth attempts are rate-limited.
- [ ] Password reset tokens are single-use and time-limited.
